The rule for k_recovery says: 'The object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT.' For the original text fence[ A ] B, the last top-level object in the text is B, so the recovered object is B. For the rewritten text fence[ A ] B C, the last top-level object is C, so the recovered object is C. Since B and C are different objects, the recovered object changes, so the answer moves.